netpair (0.1.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * netpair ps: add a header row and a HOST-PID column. Processes run in the
    pair's own PID namespace, so the PIDs shown by ps (now NS-PID) never
    existed on the host; HOST-PID is resolved from /proc via NSpid so it can
    be used with regular host tools (kill, strace, ...). Rows are sorted by
    PID, and already-exited processes show "-".
  * netpair kill: add --signal (name such as TERM, or a number) to send
    signals other than SIGKILL, e.g. for a graceful stop. Signalling an
    already-exited process is reported instead of claiming success.
  * netpair create/status: report the manager's host PID in CLI output and
    in the state file (manager_host_pid), instead of only its in-pair PID.

 -- Nicolas Cisco <nicolas@nckweb.com.ar>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:30:00 +0000

netpair (0.1.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a wire-protocol handshake: the manager reports its protocol version
    in "status". Upgrading the package does not restart the managers of
    already-running pairs, so an old manager could not serve attached
    "netpair run" (or connect auto-discovery) and failed with the cryptic
    "unknown op: wait". "netpair run" and "netpair connect" now detect this
    and say to recreate the pair, and "netpair doctor" lists existing pairs
    with their manager protocol version and warns on mismatches.

 -- Nicolas Cisco <nicolas@nckweb.com.ar>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:35:00 +0000

netpair (0.1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * netpair run is now blocking by default: it forwards stdin, merges the
    process's stdout/stderr (in order) onto the terminal, and exits with the
    process's exit code. Ctrl-C terminates the process; a second signal
    exits the client immediately. Add --daemon for the previous detached
    behaviour (output keeps going to <pair>.log, managed by ps/kill).
  * Manager protocol: 'exec' now streams stdio over the pair socket (JSON
    ack, then raw bytes, half-close on stdin EOF); new 'wait' op returns
    the exit code once the process is reaped. The old one-shot 'exec' used
    to buffer all output in the response and was unused.
  * 'ps' exit-code reporting is now race-free.

 -- Nicolas Cisco <nicolas@nckweb.com.ar>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:20:00 +0000

netpair (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * pasta AppArmor profile: add the required 'userns,' rule. Since the
    profile is loaded, it decides by itself whether pasta may create a user
    namespace — the restriction sysctls only gate unconfined programs. The
    0.1.1 profile therefore broke pasta on machines where it got loaded
    ("Couldn't create user namespace: Permission denied") even with
    apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=0.
  * netpair doctor: warn when the installed pasta profile lacks the userns
    rule, and explain the stale-profile failure mode in the remedy hint.
  * netpair create: also recognise "Couldn't create user namespace" as a
    userns denial so the remedy hint is printed.
  * Add --verbose/-v (and NETPAIR_VERBOSE=1): stream the pair log to stderr
    while create waits for pasta/manager, and mention the pair log in docs.
  * netpair list: report pairs whose state cannot be loaded instead of
    silently skipping them.

 -- Nicolas Cisco <nicolas@nckweb.com.ar>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:05:00 +0000

netpair (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship a pasta AppArmor profile (usr.bin.pasta). Ubuntu 24.04 restricts
    unprivileged user namespaces (apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1)
    and pasta can only create its namespace while running under a profile.
    The profile is loaded on install and at boot.
  * netpair create: detect pasta exiting early (zombie-aware liveness) and
    surface pasta's own error output from the per-pair pasta log.
  * netpair create: disable pasta's default 'auto' port forwarding in all
    directions (-t/-u/-T/-U none) so pairs stay isolated until the
    respective 'netpair connect'.
  * Fix DNS inside pairs: pasta inherits the host resolv.conf, whose
    127.0.0.53 systemd-resolved stub is unusable inside the namespace; the
    manager now bind-mounts a corrected copy (private to the namespace).
  * Add 'netpair doctor' for environment diagnostics (pasta, apparmor
    restriction, upstream DNS, live namespace probes).

 -- Nicolas Cisco <nicolas@nckweb.com.ar>  Mon, 20 Oct 2026 12:35:00 +0000

netpair (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.

 -- Nicolas Cisco <nicolas@nckweb.com.ar>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:50:00 +0000
